<title>GERMANY: Merck's Argentine unit buys pharma group Volpino.</title>
<headline>Merck's Argentine unit buys pharma group Volpino.</headline>
<dateline>DARMSTADT, Germany 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German pharmaceutical group Merck KGaA said on Monday that its Argentine unit Merck Quimica Argentinien SAIC had bought 100 percent of the Argentine pharmaceutical group Volpino.</p>
<p>Volpino had a turnover of around $13 million in 1995 and Merck said in a statement that its product range fitted well with that of Merck.</p>
<p>Merck's Argentine subsidiary had a turnover in 1996 of around $28 million, Merck said, and the acquisition would give Merck a market share of one percent in Argentina.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
